WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.440
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.990
I'm the new sales department hire
starting today, Michiru Amatsuki!

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.490
Nice to meet you all!

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.110
Come on, give us a bit more!

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:14.700
Huh?

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.990
Got any hobbies or talents?

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.820
Wha-?!

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.620
Well... uh...

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:20.910
I like to bead rooks...

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.500
<i>Ack! Wait, that's not right!</i>

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.500
And uh, I like to go for watch, walk TV...

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.170
<i>Ack! I keep mixing up my words!</i>

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.090
So...

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.380
<i>S-sir?!</i>

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.510
You're our new recruit who's going
to really get in and mix things up, then!

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.020
<i>Oh my, thanks for covering for me!</i>

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.990
<i>So this is what office-casual
at a Tokyo office is like, huh?</i>

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.120
<i>All these metropolitan gals with their
work-time and night-time double personas.</i>

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.580
<i>So gorgeous...</i>

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.130
<i>But from here on I'm one of them!</i>

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.590
<i>Wait! But I don't have anything nice to wear!</i>

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.010
<i>What am I gonna do?!</i>

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:46.140
"Coordinating outfits for a week in Marunouchi"...

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.390
<i>They're how much now?!</i>

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.360
<i>Do I really need five outfits to last in a Tokyo office...?</i>

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.900
<i>At this rate I won't even last a week...</i>

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.950
Ahhh, what am I gonna do?

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.910
Whoa! Hey welcome back.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:02.620
Ahhh, what am I gonna do?

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.490
Uh... is that you, Nao-san?

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.620
What happened to that wrinkly look
you had going yesterday?

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.160
Those were just my veg-out clothes!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.080
I told you I worked in apparel, right?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:17.170
You've gotta help me!
I don't have anything to wear to work!

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.930
But I don't know what to buy either...

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.850
And I want to look like hot stuff for a whole week!

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.520
Just a week? I'm shooting for a lifetime.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.270
Teach me your ways!

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.600
Well, I dunno...

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.310
I'll pay you back with drinks!

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.440
H-hey now, I'm not that much of a lush, 'kay?!

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.440
Shochu! All you can drink!

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.440
Come, my pupil!

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:40.950
<i>Wait, that worked?!</i>

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.610
Drinking your troubles away with shochu,

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.830
though; you sure are something Michiru.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.200
It was half off so I couldn't resist...

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.960
Falling for those discounts
means you're easily manipulated.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.370
<i>How am I the easily manipulated one?!</i>

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.460
Well, tonight it's chu-hi at home then!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.460
"Chu-hi"?

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.470
It's short for shochu highball!

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.550
We call drinks mixed with soda water highballs!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.060
And a highball made with shochu is a shochu highball!

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.560
But that's too long, so "chu-hi!"

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.480
Wow!

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.210
There are all sorts of flavored chu-hi these days,

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.110
but back then it was just shochu and soda water.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:22.900
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.410
Now let me show you the best way to make them!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.080
First you drop some ice in the glass with the shochu...

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.370
Then you stir it up real good!

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.500
You do this first, and get the glass
and shochu nice and chilled!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.670
As it chills, the ice melts away right?

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.510
So you fill it right back up with more ice!

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:46.550
Then you pour in some cold soda water nice and slow!

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.010
Mix it up nice and carefully,
not letting all the carbonation escape, and...

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.520
You've got yourself a perfect chu-hi!

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.020
Here's to finishing another workday!

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.520
Cheers!

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.660
Whew! That soda really packs a punch!

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.410
You down it so heartily!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:13.870
By making sure it's all chilled beforehand,
the ice doesn't melt while you drink.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.670
It doesn't get watered down while you drink,
so it's good to the very last drop!

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:25.420
At the pace you drink, does it even have time to melt?

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.180
Huh?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.680
What's with the sudden fashion
kick though, Michiru-chan?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.310
Oh...

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:37.690
I just want to have something to wear that fits in
with how splendid my coworkers look.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.940
I really wasn't ready for Tokyo to be quite so trendy.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.490
Not all of Tokyo is like that; you know.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.280
There are more downtown sorts of areas
and places where all the old men go to drink.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.950
There are lots of great less-famous places too.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.620
"Famous places"...

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.960
Now that you mention it,
I still haven't even seen Sky Tree!

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.540
Sky Tree! Have you two been up Sky Tree before?!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:06.300
The view of the night skyline must be
just incredible from up there, huh?

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.970
Got someone you wanna go up there with?

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:08.590
Huh?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.720
Yeah, that sort of thing is for couples.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.310
N-no, I don't...

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:18.020
I mean, maybe someday, I hope. But...

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.730
Maybe you all do, but-

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.860
Nope!

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:26.740
Isn't Sky Tree a bit too high to really
enjoy the night skyline anyway?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.740
I doubt you can see anything but rooftops really.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.490
Nooo...

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.580
Where would you go then, Kae?

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:34.990
Hmm, well...

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:38.750
A fancy bar up on the top floor
of a big hotel is always nice.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.500
Or a night cruise to see the skyline
from the sea might be romantic, too...

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.470
I need something to go with these drinks.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.680
Here we are. It's just leftovers, but here,

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.020
have some ham, egg, and potato salad.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.390
Oh nice. Got that real homely,
downtown joint sort of feel.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:03.060
What kind of feel is that exactly?

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:07.490
Those retro sorts of places with red lanterns
and split curtains and stuff.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.660
They say the chu-hi came from places like that you know.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:14.450
Heya barkeep! What sorta specials
you got for me today?

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.660
Well, today...

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:21.670
We have steak tips. Cooked up with some butter
and soy sauce to make it extra rich.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.000
Do eat up before it gets cold and hard!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.670
Oh I will, I will!

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:37.720
Mmm! It's so nice and hot, washing it down
with that tonic water and shochu is sheer bliss!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.940
Hey there, girly, you make that drink look divine!

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.600
<i>Has she actually been to a place like this before...?</i>

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.110
Wait!

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.570
Can you get to giving me some clothing tips?
Please, oh teacher!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.900
Ah, right!

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.320
Now then, watch and behold!

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:58.620
The charismatic apparel pro, Nao Kiriyama,
will find you the perfect outfits.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.120
On today's fashion show!

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:07.000
So grown up and ready for work!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.710
That natural look will capture hearts!

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.130
So sweet and lovable!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:13.800
What's with the face?

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.640
This is embarrassing!

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:20.350
I was hoping for, you know... something more natural
like this, that doesn't stand out too much.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.640
I'm not all that worried about the price...

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.060
Hmm, well then.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.480
This sort of look probably suits you best.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:29.900
Wow...

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:33.530
Just pick whatever jumps out at you.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:38.160
In the end, whatever you want to wear most
on any given day is what will look best on you.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.160
<i>Nao-san looks like a completely
different person than before...</i>

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.120
Yeah. That there might be best.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.960
Y-you think so?

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.090
You can have that.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.430
What?! N-no, I don't mean to-

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.180
Nah, it's fine. I've never even worn it.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:01.430
I'll say, though, it really is fun
finding a look that fits someone.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.480
Thanks for reminding me of that.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.980
That's basically why I got into
this line of work to begin with.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.940
You just gave me the motivation I needed
to get through work tomorrow.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.900
My, how touching.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:16.450
This must be a new drunk version of you, huh, Nao-chan?

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.410
Oh, give me a break!

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.080
Shochu highballs... basically where all
chu-hi started from.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:31.460
Getting back to enjoying things
from their roots isn't so bad, huh?

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.720
Good morning!

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:45.230
<i>I... hope I'm not pushing it too much...
The girls did say this looked good on me though, so...</i>

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:47.440
Good morning, Amatsuki-san.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.480
What's a young'un like you doing in so early?

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.900
Oh, I just woke up extra early this morning.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.450
<i>Maybe I can pull this off?</i>

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.370
<i>With this, I'm finally a Tokyoite myself...</i>

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.870
<i>I'm one of those pretty office ladies now...</i>

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.000
Hello! Thank you very much for your 'coal'!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:11.500
<i>"Coal!"</i>

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.510
J-just one moment please...

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:19.510
<i>"The new recruit who's going to really get in
and mix things up," huh?</i>

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.350
But still she persisted...

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.060
Yes, Michiru too returned to her roots.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:01.530
Chu-hi aren't always made with shochu,
but often with vodka too, you know.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:05.780
It's got less of a kick to it, so it goes really well
with lemon or grapefruit.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:10.330
Even with shochu though, if you use sugarless types
of shochu, it goes well with fruity flavors.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.370
Mmm, it's so good.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.130
Here's to another night!
